7.3 Describe the snapshot with dataspice
Allow about three minutes. Four prepared CSV files under data/metadata/health-wellbeing/ record the title and licence, creator, download link, and variables. The row for n in attributes.csv says that each row of the data describes one study and n is the sample size within that study. The teaching snapshot has 29 rows and five variables (Harrer et al., n.d.).
dataspice combines the CSV files into a Schema.org JSON-LD record (Boettiger et al. 2026). The excerpt shows the title, licence, download link, and the entry for n, so you can see that its meaning and unit survive the export.

source("pipelines/workshop_support.R")
source_dir &lt;- file.path("data", "metadata", "health-wellbeing")
metadata_dir &lt;- file.path(workshop_output_dir(), "metadata")
dir.create(metadata_dir, recursive = TRUE, showWarnings = FALSE)

templates &lt;- file.path(
  source_dir, c("biblio.csv", "creators.csv", "access.csv", "attributes.csv")
)
stopifnot(all(file.copy(templates, metadata_dir, overwrite = TRUE)))
dataspice::write_spice(path = metadata_dir)

record &lt;- jsonlite::read_json(file.path(metadata_dir, "dataspice.json"))
excerpt &lt;- record[c("name", "license", "distribution")]
excerpt$variableMeasured &lt;- Filter(
  function(variable) variable$name == "n", record$variableMeasured
)
jsonlite::toJSON(excerpt, auto_unbox = TRUE, pretty = TRUE)

{
  "name": "HealthWellbeing teaching snapshot",
  "license": "https://opensource.org/license/mit",
  "distribution": [
    {
      "type": "DataDownload",
      "name": "HealthWellbeing teaching data (R data file)",
      "contentUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MathiasHarrer/dmetar/38c9b9bb5f85ea49de33e5d2536f6544d5268517/data/HealthWellbeing.rda",
      "encodingFormat": "application/octet-stream"
    }
  ],
  "variableMeasured": [
    {
      "type": "PropertyValue",
      "unitText": "observations",
      "name": "n",
      "description": "Sample size within the study"
    }
  ]
} 


This record describes the verified teaching file. The link resolves to a particular upstream revision. Keep the source and licence notice in data/raw/ with the metadata. The DOI in biblio.csv identifies the original review. Check for placeholder coverage fields before publishing the generated record.
The repository’s reviewed copy omits empty publication and coverage fields and writes @type, which has the same meaning as type under the Schema.org context. The full record below is the repository copy. The assessment fetches the pinned revision of that record.






